# Apple Magic Keyboard (05ac:0320): expose the Globe/Fn key as KEY_F20 so
# Wispr Flow can use it as a dictation key on X11.
#
# The keyboard's HID descriptor declares Globe/Fn on usage page 0x00ff,
# usage 0x0003. hid_apple initially maps that usage to KEY_FN (464), which
# is outside X11's keycode range. Remap the HID scancode before X11 sees it.
# `showkey --scancodes` prints translated console codes, not the HID
# scancodes that udev's keyboard builtin needs. Its 0x6f was misleading.
#
# F20 is chosen because it is in range for X11 (keycodes cap at 255): the real
# KEY_DICTATE (0x24a, 586) would need keycode 594 and can never reach an X
# client. xprofile/i3 relabel keycode 198 to F20 for Wispr Flow.
#
# Not Right Alt: Alt_R is in X11 mod1, so every Globe press also held Alt down
# system-wide, and Firefox binds Alt aggressively (Alt+Left/Right history, Alt+D
# address bar, menu mnemonics), which dropped/duplicated dictated text.
evdev:input:b0003v05ACp0320*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_00ff0003=f20
